ormed hourly and that each THON Weekend receives a newly designed dance with unique moves and words.","source_url":"https://www.psu.edu/news/story/thon-2020-big-reveal","source_title":"THON 2020: The Big Reveal | Penn State University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Takes place during THON Weekend; participation and spectator arrangements are event-specific.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"penn-state-homecoming-parade","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Penn State Homecoming Parade","title":"Follow the Homecoming Parade route","subtitle":"University Park and downtown State College","notes":"Check the current Homecoming schedule, then watch the parade as it travels through campus and downtown before the shrine program.","short_summary":"A long-running Homecoming procession joining students, alumni, and the town.","evidence_claim":"Penn State says its community has observed Homecoming regularly since 1920 and identifies the parade as one of its oldest traditions.","source_url":"https://www.psu.edu/news/campus-life/story/history-penn-state-homecoming-remembrance-reflection-and-revelry","source_title":"The history of Penn State Homecoming: Remembrance, reflection and revelry | Penn State University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Annual Homecoming scheduling and route details vary; use the current official program.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"nittany-lion-shrine-photo-bookend","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Nittany Lion Shrine Photo Bookend","title":"Take the Lion Shrine photo twice","subtitle":"First day and graduation-day photo ritual","notes":"Photograph the shrine from the surrounding plaza on your first day, then revisit in cap and gown at graduation without climbing the sculpture.","short_summary":"A documented before-and-after photo ritual framing a Penn State degree.","evidence_claim":"Penn State’s visitor guide describes a tradition of students photographing themselves on the Lion as freshmen and again in caps and gowns at graduation.","source_url":"https://studentaffairs.psu.edu/sites/default/files/Visiting%20Clubs%20Guide%202020.pdf","source_title":"Penn State Visiting Clubs Guide","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use the surrounding public area and respect any posted monument-access guidance.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"schreyer-honors-college-gong","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Schreyer Honors College Gong","title":"Ring the thesis-completion gong","subtitle":"Schreyer Honors College thesis tradition","notes":"Schreyer Scholars who complete their thesis may ring the gong; visitors can spot it at the Medals Ceremony and in college displays.","short_summary":"A thesis milestone marked by one ceremonial gong strike.","evidence_claim":"Schreyer Honors College states that, since 2000, only Scholars who have completed their thesis may strike its gong.","source_url":"https://www.shc.psu.edu/about/history-traditions/index.cfm","source_title":"History & Traditions | Schreyer Honors College","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Ringing is limited to Scholars who have completed their thesis; ceremony access varies.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"old-willow-replanting","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Old Willow Replanting","title":"Look for the Old Willow successor","subtitle":"Old Main lawn","notes":"Pause by the Old Main lawn to see the current willow and l